# pnpm's default (node-linker=isolated) builds each package's node_modules
# out of per-package symlinks into the central .pnpm store. Most tooling in
# this repo handles that fine, but Expo/React Native's native-build
# toolchain (expo-modules-autolinking's Gradle/CocoaPods integration,
# Metro) resolves modules the way plain npm/yarn-classic does — walking a
# real, flat node_modules tree — and can resolve a *different* copy of a
# transitive dependency (e.g. expo-modules-core) at different points in the
# Android Gradle build than at JS-level autolinking config generation,
# producing exactly the "generated Java references a class/package that
# doesn't exist in the version actually on the compile classpath" failure
# class (e.g. `expo.core.ExpoModulesPackage` — the pre-SDK-45 class name —
# imported by generated code even though installed expo-modules-core is
# 2.x, whose real class is `expo.modules.ExpoModulesPackage`).
#
# This is Expo's own documented fix for pnpm monorepos
# (https://docs.expo.dev/guides/monorepos/#pnpm): hoist to a single flat
# node_modules tree so every tool — pnpm itself, Metro, and the Android/iOS
# native build tooling — resolves the exact same physical copy of every
# package. Requires a clean reinstall to take effect (switching
# node-linker doesn't retroactively restructure an existing isolated
# install).
node-linker=hoisted
